# The bug-finding checks only. Style is the compiler's job here and the house rules' job in review; this
# file exists to catch defects, so a check that argues about taste is off rather than argued with.
#
# This tree is 1999 C, so the noise profile differs from a modern C++ project: the exclusions below are
# checks that fire in the hundreds on code that is correct as written. If one starts finding real
# defects, turn it back on -- none of them are off because the findings were tedious.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  misc-*,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-reserved-identifier,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.strcpy,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-unused-parameters,
  -misc-predictable-rand,
  -misc-use-internal-linkage,
  -misc-no-recursion,
  -bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition,
  -bugprone-switch-missing-default-case,
  -bugprone-branch-clone,
  -bugprone-float-loop-counter,
  -clang-analyzer-security.FloatLoopCounter,
  -bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion,
  -bugprone-signed-char-misuse,
  -bugprone-suspicious-string-compare,
  -bugprone-suspicious-include,
  -performance-no-int-to-ptr,
  -performance-type-promotion-in-math-fn

# Our own sources. external/navlib is vendored from its own repository and is fixed there.
HeaderFilterRegex: 'src/'

# bugprone-narrowing-conversions: 121 findings in four files. Quake 2 moves between int and float
#   constantly and by design, and every vec3_t index is an int into a float array.
# bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: every (x, y, z) and (min, max) triple trips it.
# bugprone-reserved-identifier: id's byte-swap helpers are named _BigShort, _LittleLong and so on.
#   Technically reserved, but renaming 1999 API to satisfy a linter buys nothing.
# clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.strcpy and DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling: 102 findings, and
#   they fire on every strcpy, sprintf and memcpy in the tree rather than on a defect. All 324 copy
#   sites were audited by hand in September 2026; a blanket "this function exists" report adds nothing.
# misc-include-cleaner: 17 findings in one file, and it disagrees with the include rules this tree
#   follows.
# misc-unused-parameters: the compiler flags already carry -Wno-unused-parameter for the same reason.
# misc-predictable-rand: the game uses rand() for gameplay, which is what it is for.
# misc-use-internal-linkage: 64 findings in one file. clang-tidy sees one translation unit, so it
#   cannot know a function is called from another one, and in a multi-TU C project that makes it a
#   structural false positive rather than a finding.
# performance-type-promotion-in-math-fn: the SDK calls the double math functions deliberately; the
#   float variants change results, and the library has to behave like the 1999 one.

# ---- Added 2026-09-14, after triaging all 468 remaining findings across both trees. Each of these
# was read in full (not sampled) and produced no defect; the checks that DID produce defects stay on
# and are listed at the bottom.
#
# bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition: the Quake 2 find-and-test idiom, `if ((e = G_Find(...)) != NULL)`
#   and `if (!(mem = ...))`, always parenthesised and either compared or negated. A census of all 90
#   sites found no bare `if (a = b)`.
# bugprone-switch-missing-default-case: closed internal sets -- rand()%N, ORIENTATION_*, level.episode,
#   MOD_* -- where falling out is the intended no-op. The one switch over untrusted input, the client
#   command byte in kpded2's sv_user.c, already has a default that kicks the client.
# bugprone-branch-clone: deliberate shared cases -- surface, weapon, classname and episode
#   enumerations, parallel guard clauses -- or verbatim id code. Worth a one-off manual run, which
#   found the AI_SideTrace yaw bug, but not worth a standing check.
# bugprone-float-loop-counter / clang-analyzer-security.FloatLoopCounter: vec3_t is float[3], so
#   world-space probe loops use float counters with exactly-representable integer steps. The same 14
#   lines reported twice -- the analyzer set is a strict subset of the bugprone one.
# bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion: an array of pointers passed to memset/fwrite/qsort
#   as void*, or the redblack API returning void* for a pointer to a stored void* slot. No pointed-to
#   size mismatch; both trees are i386.
# bugprone-signed-char-misuse: all sites correct as written. COM_Parse's scanner must treat a high-bit
#   byte the way the unpatchable retail client does; two more are neutralised by the `c &= 127` on the
#   next line; one flags MSG_ReadChar's deliberate (signed char) protocol cast, which is the fix rather
#   than the bug. The check also cannot see the one shape that would matter here, a plain char passed
#   to the ctype functions, because it inspects assignments and subscripts, not call arguments.
# bugprone-suspicious-string-compare: every site is `if (strcmp(a, b))` used as a boolean, which reads
#   only the sign and is correct. Nothing in either tree stores a compare result in a narrow type or
#   tests it against literal 1 or -1, and the genuine ordering uses already spell out `> 0` / `< 0`.
# misc-no-recursion: recursion is not a defect here. All four chains are depth-bounded -- by a flag
#   cleared before the recursive call, by the memory record the callee creates, or by the static item
#   table -- and SV_Physics_Toss's self-call is dead, since MOVETYPE_TOSS_SLIDE is never assigned.
# bugprone-suspicious-include: net_udp.c includes qcommon/net_common.c, R1Q2's mechanism for sharing
#   net code between the Linux and Win32 socket layers. Deliberate and permanent.
# performance-no-int-to-ptr: mmap's MAP_FAILED comparison and the ELF load address from
#   dl_iterate_phdr, which is an integer by API. Neither pointer is dereferenced.
#
# KEPT ON deliberately, with what each returned in the 2026-09-14 pass:
# bugprone-integer-division -- the vote-ban majority threshold and the Bagman cash-bag delay ratio.
# clang-analyzer-deadcode.DeadStores -- a disabled length clamp guarding a 64 KiB stack buffer.
# bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-conversion -- a /0 CIDR mask reaching a shift by 32, pak files
#   silently reloaded as pak0, and trigger_gravity truncating "0.5" to 0.
# clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange -- a means-of-death constant passed as a qboolean.
# bugprone-signal-handler -- the SIGTERM handler running the whole shutdown from signal context.
# misc-redundant-expression, bugprone-unsafe-functions -- no findings, but cheap and they guard a real
#   defect class (`a && a`, and setbuf reappearing in the stdio setup).
